<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 266 0 R
/T (What is Clinical Research? Clinical research is the process of studying medicines, treatments, medical devices, and other health care approaches in people. The goal is to gather reliable information about their safety and effectiveness.)
/E (What is Clinical Research? Clinical research is the process of studying medicines, treatments, medical devices, and other health care approaches in people. The goal is to gather reliable information about their safety and effectiveness.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 266 0 R
/T (A clinical trial is a structured research study involving human participants. Each trial follows a detailed research plan, called a protocol that describes who may participate, the procedures that will take place, the information collected, and how participants will be monitored throughout the trial. Participation in a trial is generally voluntary, and the informed-consent process explains the study, its procedures, foreseeable risks and potential benefits, alternatives, confidentiality, and participants' rights to discontinue participation.)
/E (A clinical trial is a structured research study involving human participants. Each trial follows a detailed research plan, called a protocol that describes who may participate, the procedures that will take place, the information collected, and how participants will be monitored throughout the trial. Participation in a trial is generally voluntary, and the informed-consent process explains the study, its procedures, foreseeable risks and potential benefits, alternatives, confidentiality, and participants' rights to discontinue participation.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
