/Title (A clinical trial is a structured research study involving human participants. Each trial follows a detailed research plan, called a protocol that describes who may participate, the procedures that will take place, the information collected, and how participants will be monitored throughout the trial. Participation in a trial is generally voluntary, and the informed-consent process explains the study, its procedures, foreseeable risks and potential benefits, alternatives, confidentiality, and participants' rights to discontinue participation.)
